; Golden expansion tests for the coverage instrumenter, one fixture per
; instrumented form - the entry-point forms plus the expression-grade
; restorations (application out-edges, pipelines, &&/|| condition arms,
; class bodies) - and the exclusions (off attributes at every level,
; excluded file, lazy guard, leaf-only functions, out-of-scope forms, a
; file with nothing to instrument). pp.exe is a standalone ppxlib driver
; linking the rewriter; each fixture .ml is expanded (with-stdout-to) or
; rejected (with-accepted-exit-codes 1, capturing the diagnostic) and
; diffed against a committed .expected golden. The goldens pin point
; indexes and byte extents - editing a fixture reshuffles them, so read
; every promoted diff. Accept intended changes with dune promote. The
; fixtures are not compiled: only pp is a module.

(executable
 (name pp)
 (modules pp)
 (libraries ppxlib windtrap_coverage_ppx))

; Expansion goldens

(rule
 (with-stdout-to
  fixture_match.actual
  (run ./pp.exe --impl %{dep:fixture_match.ml})))

(rule
 (alias runtest)
 (action
  (diff fixture_match.expected fixture_match.actual)))

(rule
